1
00:00:00,015 --> 00:00:00,683
You're a tiny

2
00:00:00,703 --> 00:00:01,908
kangaroo ancestor,

3
00:00:01,928 --> 00:00:02,645
and your forest

4
00:00:02,665 --> 00:00:03,851
is disappearing.

5
00:00:03,871 --> 00:00:04,726
You climb and hop

6
00:00:04,746 --> 00:00:05,957
through the rainforest.

7
00:00:05,977 --> 00:00:07,132
But Australia slowly

8
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:07,895
dries out.

9
00:00:07,915 --> 00:00:08,708
Your trees turn

10
00:00:08,728 --> 00:00:10,129
into open grassland.

11
00:00:10,149 --> 00:00:11,216
Your descendants become

12
00:00:11,236 --> 00:00:12,371
expert hoppers.

13
00:00:12,391 --> 00:00:14,008
Springy tendons store energy,

14
00:00:14,028 --> 00:00:15,008
so speed costs

15
00:00:15,028 --> 00:00:15,999
almost nothing.

16
00:00:16,019 --> 00:00:16,811
Everywhere else,

17
00:00:16,831 --> 00:00:18,173
hoppers stay tiny.

18
00:00:18,193 --> 00:00:18,948
Your babies are

19
00:00:18,968 --> 00:00:20,677
born jellybean-sized.

20
00:00:20,697 --> 00:00:21,752
They crawl alone into

21
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:22,880
your pouch to grow.

22
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:23,817
You can even pause

23
00:00:23,837 --> 00:00:24,767
the next baby until

24
00:00:24,787 --> 00:00:25,859
the pouch is free.

25
00:00:25,879 --> 00:00:26,347
That's how a

26
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:27,684
tiny forest hopper

27
00:00:27,704 --> 00:00:29,254
became the kangaroo.
